      es: "The Amazighs, long called Berbers, are the indigenous peoples of North Africa, present on the land that is Morocco since prehistory. From the Numidian and Mauretanian kingdoms of antiquity to the great medieval confederations of Awraba, Barghawata, Masmuda, Sanhaja and Zenata, they founded states, gave the country two of its greatest dynasties, the Almoravids and the Almohads, and resisted Arabisation as well as, later, the French and Spanish protectorates. Their identity was inscribed in the Constitution for the first time in 2011.",
