      en: "The Amazigh calendar has its own high points, from Yennayer, the New Year, whose first day corresponds to the 14th of January of the Gregorian calendar and which was erected into an official national holiday in 2023, to the moussems and the seasonal festivals that punctuate the life of the villages: the marriage festival of Imilchil in the High Atlas, the almond-blossom festival of Tafraoute in the Anti-Atlas, and, on the great stage of Agadir, the Timitar festival, which places the Amazigh music at the heart of its programme.",
